Input file 2
#######################################################################################################################################
[eq]            [initial]
20              2

[viscosity]     [Pr]
1.0e-3          0.72

[order]         [flux]          [diffusion]     [shock_capture]     [av_c]          [av_kappa]
3               0               1               1                   1.0             2.0

[time_type]     [dt_type]       [t_order]       [t_fixed]           [CFL]           [t_final]       
0               0               2               0.001               0.1             0.20                          

[matrix]        [pre]
0               0
#######################################################################################################################################
[problem]
-> eq: 10(linear advection, a = 1), 11(linear advection-diffusion, a = 1, D = viscosity), 20(euler), 21(euler + viscous terms)
-> initial: 0(sine density wave), 1(constant state), 2(Sod shock tube at x = 0.5)

[physical values]
-> viscosity: diffusivity D for eq = 11; constant dynamic viscosity for eq = 21
-> Pr: Prandtl number

[spatial discretization]
-> order: solution order
-> flux: 0(LLF)
-> diffusion: 0(BR1), 1(BR2), also used for the artificial-viscosity gradient
-> shock_capture: 0(off), 1(Persson density sensor + C0 artificial viscosity); must be 0 for eq = 10 or 11
-> av_c: maximum viscosity coefficient, eps_max = av_c*(h/p)*(abs(u)+c)
-> av_kappa: half-width of the smooth activation interval in log10(sensor)

[time_integration]
-> time_type: 0(explicit-euler,RK), 1(implicit-BDF)
-> dt_type: 0(CFL), 1(fixed)
-> t_order: time stepping order
-> CFL: CFL number
-> t_final: final physical time

[linear solver]
-> matrix(matrix solver): 0(GMRES)
-> pre(preconditioner): 0(none), 1(Block-Jacobi)
#######################################################################################################################################
